<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Registered Office: Section 12 of Companies Act</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Under S.12, every company must maintain a registered office in India for all communications. Address appears on MCA Master Data, letterheads, signage. Clause II of MOA specifies the state. Any change must be reported via prescribed forms. Non-compliance: Rs 1,000/day (S.12(9)).</p><p>Complexity depends on where you move: within-city = Board Resolution + INC-22 only. Across ROC = Regional Director approval via INC-23. Inter-state = MOA amendment + creditor consent + newspaper publication.</p><p><strong>CRITICAL Delhi Update:</strong> MCA notification effective 16 Feb 2026 bifurcated Delhi ROC into ROC South Delhi and ROC Central Delhi. Cross-district moves may now be inter-ROC transfers requiring INC-23 and RD approval.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Change in Registered Office in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>ROC Bifurcation (Feb 2026):</strong> ROC NCT Delhi → ROC South Delhi + ROC Central Delhi. District-wise mapping. Cross-district = inter-ROC.</p><p><strong>INC-22:</strong> All scenarios. Notice of change. 15-60 days depending on scenario. NOC + utility bill required.</p><p><strong>INC-23:</strong> Inter-ROC and inter-state only. Regional Director application. Creditor declarations. Newspaper publication.</p><p><strong>Penalty:</strong> Rs 1,000/day for late INC-22 (S.12(9)). Strike-off risk (S.248).</p>

                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="column-image">
                <div class="illustration-placeholder">
                    <div class="illustration-icon" style="max-width:240px;">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 200 180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <!-- Building / Tribunal -->
